{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**Chasing Cherry Blossoms in Tokyo and Kyoto**\n\nMy recent trip to Japan was a whirlwind of ancient traditions and futuristic wonders. It began in the electric heart of Tokyo, where neon lights painted the night sky in Shibuya. The energy was palpable, yet amidst the chaos, I found pockets of serenity in the Meiji Shrine, where towering trees blocked out the city's hum.\n\nThe journey south to Kyoto offered a stark, beautiful contrast. Wandering through the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove felt like stepping into another world, the towering stalks swaying gently in the breeze. The highlight, however, was visiting Fushimi Inari-taisha at sunrise. Thousands of vermilion torii gates created a winding path up the mountain, offering a spiritual climb that left me breathless.\n\nFood was a revelation. From steaming bowls of ramen in narrow alleyways to the delicate artistry of a traditional kaiseki meal, every bite told a story. I learned that patience is key, whether waiting for the perfect sushi rice or watching the slow dance of cherry blossoms falling like pink snow.\n\nJapan is a place where the past and future coexist seamlessly. The politeness of the locals, the precision of the trains, and the deep respect for nature made every moment memorable. As my flight took off, I realized I wasn't just leaving a country; I was leaving a feeling of harmony that I will carry with me forever. If you ever have the chance to go, take it. You won't regret it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.22237068}, {"token": "asing", "logprob": -1.6434433}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -0.0130142355}, {"token": " Bloss", "logprob": -0.00054117775}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.5036406}, {"token": " Tokyo", "logprob": -2.984268}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.2532139}, {"token": " Kyoto", "logprob"